                <pb facs="1100" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Business Tax/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-06T17:00:00+08:00">March 6, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 6—9:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>107. Legation’s 93, March 1, 3 p.m., paragraph 3.</p>
                <p>Following from American Consulate at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 5, 3 p.m. I am informed by the Ministry of Finance that reports
                            appearing in Chinese press concerning procedure for collection of
                            business tax are premature. I have been promised copy of procedure when
                            it is promulgated.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
